NOTES ON THIS LICENSE (do not remove; retained for clarity)

1. Scope. This MIT license covers the code, configuration files, scripts,
   tests, expected outputs and documentation authored for the MIRAGE-DoH
   reproducibility artifact and contained in this repository. It does NOT
   cover:

     a. The CIC-DoH2023 dataset, which is released by the Canadian Institute
        for Cybersecurity at the University of New Brunswick under CC-BY 4.0.
        The dataset is not redistributed in this repository; it is fetched
        by data/download_datasets.py from its official public source.

     b. The Gen-C-DDD-2022 dataset, which is released by the same institute
        under CC-BY 4.0. Same treatment as (a).

     c. The 1 MB toy dataset in data/toy_dataset/. It is a derivative of the
        two datasets above and is distributed under the same CC-BY 4.0 terms,
        with attribution recorded in data/README_data.md and
        data/toy_dataset/README.md.

     d. Any third-party Python packages installed via requirements.txt or
        environment.yml. Each package retains its own license; a reviewer
        should consult the package metadata (pip show <pkg>) for details.

     e. The Intel Loihi 2 and NVIDIA A100 hardware references. These are
        proprietary products of Intel Corporation and NVIDIA Corporation
        respectively. The hardware_simulation/ directory contains software
        that reproduces the *trends* of measurements taken on that hardware;
        it does not reproduce or reverse-engineer the hardware itself.

2. Attribution. If you use this artifact in academic work, please cite the
   associated paper (see README.md §11) and reference Chapter 3 of the thesis
   for the derivation of Equations 1-31.

3. No warranty for measured claims. The MIT warranty disclaimer applies with
   particular force to the quantitative results in expected_outputs/: those
   numbers are the values reported in the thesis on the thesis testbed, and
   are reproduced in this artifact under the determinism and tolerance
   conditions stated in REPRODUCIBILITY_CHECKLIST.md §7-§8. No warranty is
   made that the same numbers will be produced on any other hardware or with
   any other dataset.

4. Author attribution. The copyright holder is listed as "The MIRAGE-DoH
   Thesis Author(s)" to keep this artifact consistent with the blind-review
   redactions in the thesis PDF. If the repository owner wishes to attribute
   the work to a named individual or to the university, edit the copyright
   line at the top of this file before the first public release. This note
   may then be deleted; the MIT grant itself does not depend on it.

5. Compatibility. MIT is compatible with the CC-BY 4.0 license of the
   datasets and with the licenses of every Python dependency in
   requirements.txt. It is also compatible with the publication venue of
   Chapter 3 (IEEE Transactions on Network and Service Management, 2026,
   DOI 10.1109/TNSM.2026.3677474), which does not require a copyleft
   license for artifacts.
